<title>UK: Ex-dividends to take 6.785 points off FTSE,Sept 23.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividends to take 6.785 points off FTSE,Sept 23.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following FTSE 100 index stockswill go ex-dividend on September 23 and analysts estimate the effect will be to take 6.785 points off the index that day.</p>
<p>							DIVIDEND     INDEX</p>
<p>							(PENCE)     EFFECT</p>
<p>		  COMPANY			  Net     Gross  Gross</p>
<p>    * BTR Plc			  5.000    --    1.150</p>
<p>    * British Aerospace	     6.250   7.813  0.195</p>
<p>    * Ladbroke Group		2.400   3.000  0.204</p>
<p>    * Legal &amp; General	     8.750  10.938  0.317</p>
<p>    * RTZ Corp			10.600    --    0.668</p>
<p>    * Shell Transport	    14.400  18.000  3.492</p>
<p>    * Tesco			   3.250   4.063  0.512</p>
<p>    * Williams Holdings	   5.800   7.250  0.247</p>
<p>NOTE: Dividends for BTR Plc and RTZ Corp are for Foreign Income Dividend only.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7954</p>
</text>
